# Lossless

> A source repo named Lossless. This wrap keeps the name and points back to the original files.

## Purpose
Give a human-readable door to fitzyracing1/Lossless so the project can be opened without guessing from the title alone.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Keep the original repo as the place for code.
2. Use this clone only to explain the idea in everyday words.
3. Send the reader back to the source for any run.

## Key ideas
- Lossless (nothing important is thrown away)
- Wrap (this page explains; it does not replace)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/Lossless
open_source()
keep_all_bits_that_matter()
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. open_source() → “go to the original repo for the files”
2. keep_all_bits_that_matter() → “do not throw away the payload the name promises to keep”

## Decisions the program makes
- If a reader needs the program → send them to the source repo
- If a reader needs the idea → stay on this listing

## What a person would notice
A named wrap that refuses to hide the original.

## Current status
Barrage clone. Source had no public one-line description at wrap time.

## Next possible steps
Open fitzyracing1/Lossless and read the README there.
